ng the sense of the House of Representatives in support of Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's initiative to transition the United States-Israel relationship toward mutual defense cooperation and joint economic investment, recognizing the contributions of Israel to joint military operations against Iran, and condemning the global rise of antisemitism.","type":"hres","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-resolution/1339"},{"bipartisan":true,"cosponsors":1,"crossPartyCosponsors":1,"id":"hr8278-119","introducedDate":"2026-04-14","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2026-09-16","text":"Received in the Senate and Read twice and referred to the Committee on Banking, Housing, and Urban Affairs."},"number":"HR 8278","policyArea":"Finance and Financial Sector","ranked":true,"stage":"passed_one_chamber","summary":"Fostering the Use of Technology to Uphold Regulatory Effectiveness in Supervision Act This bill requires specified federal financial agencies to assess their technological capabilities and procurement practices. Specifically, agencies (the Federal Reserve Board, the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau, the Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation, the Department of the Treasury, the Office of the...","summarySource":"crs","title":"Fostering the Use of Technology to Uphold Regulatory Effectiveness in Supervision Act","type":"hr","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/8278"},{"bipartisan":false,"cosponsors":3,"crossPartyCosponsors":0,"id":"hr8155-119","introducedDate":"2026-03-27","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2026-03-27","text":"Referred to the House Committee on the Judiciary."},"number":"HR 8155","policyArea":"International Affairs","ranked":true,"stage":"introduced","summary":"Amends the Foreign Agents Registration Act to require disclosures on informational materials identifying whether foreign principals are supervised, directed, owned, controlled, financed, or subsidized by covered nations or their governmental actors.","summarySource":"ai","title":"Foreign Propaganda Transparency Act","type":"hr","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/8155"},{"bipartisan":false,"cosponsors":0,"crossPartyCosponsors":0,"id":"hr8090-119","introducedDate":"2026-03-25","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2026-03-25","text":"Referred to the House Committee on Financial Services."},"number":"HR 8090","policyArea":"Finance and Financial Sector","ranked":true,"stage":"introduced","summary":"Requires the Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation and National Credit Union Administration to analyze whether insurance coverage for covered transaction accounts held by businesses, nonprofits, and municipalities should be increased, and to assess economic impacts and safety implications.","summarySource":"ai","title":"To require the Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation and the National Credit Union Administration to carry out an analysis to determine whether insurance coverage should be raised on covered transaction accounts, and for other purposes.","type":"hr","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/8090"},{"bipartisan":false,"cosponsors":0,"crossPartyCosponsors":0,"id":"hr7586-119","introducedDate":"2026-02-13","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2026-03-02","text":"Referred to the Subcommittee on Economic Opportunity."},"number":"HR 7586","policyArea":"Housing and Community Development","ranked":true,"stage":"introduced","summary":"Requires federal agencies to issue guidance within 180 days restricting the sale of single-family homes financed through federal programs to large institutional investors, while promoting sales to individual owner-occupants, with exceptions for build-to-rent properties and similar arrangements.","summarySource":"ai","title":"American Families First Act","type":"hr","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/7586"},{"bipartisan":false,"cosponsors":2,"crossPartyCosponsors":0,"id":"hr7237-119","introducedDate":"2026-01-23","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2026-01-23","text":"Referred to the House Committee on Energy and Commerce."},"number":"HR 7237","policyArea":"Health","ranked":true,"stage":"introduced","summary":"Amends the Public Health Service Act to require chemical abortion providers receiving federal funds to provide women with FDA-approved drug labels and highlighted warnings at least 24 hours before the procedure, and establishes federal funding withholding and private lawsuits for violations.","summarySource":"ai","title":"Chemical Abortion Risk Awareness Act","type":"hr","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/7237"},{"bipartisan":false,"cosponsors":1,"crossPartyCosponsors":0,"id":"hr6541-119","introducedDate":"2025-12-09","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2026-02-25","text":"Placed on the Union Calendar, Calendar No. 451."},"number":"HR 6541","policyArea":"Finance and Financial Sector","ranked":true,"stage":"reported","summary":"Regulation A+ Improvement Act of 2025 This bill increases the aggregate dollar limit of certain securities offerings exempt from registration requirements (i.e., Regulation A+ offerings) from $50 million annually to $150 million annually, adjusted in future years for inflation.","summarySource":"crs","title":"Regulation A+ Improvement Act of 2025","type":"hr","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/6541"},{"bipartisan":false,"cosponsors":0,"crossPartyCosponsors":0,"id":"hr5808-119","introducedDate":"2025-10-21","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-10-21","text":"Referred to the Committee on Foreign Affairs, and in addition to the Committee on the Judiciary, for a period to be subsequently determined by the Speaker, in each case for consideration of such provisions as fall within the jurisdiction of the committee concerned."},"number":"HR 5808","policyArea":"International Affairs","ranked":true,"stage":"introduced","summary":"Requires the President to impose sanctions on Nigerian officials who promoted, enacted, or tolerated religious violence, and mandates designating Nigeria as a Country of Particular Concern for violations of religious freedom.","summarySource":"ai","title":"Nigeria Religious Freedom Accountability Act of 2025","type":"hr","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/5808"},{"bipartisan":true,"cosponsors":15,"crossPartyCosponsors":7,"id":"hr4989-119","introducedDate":"2025-08-15","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-08-15","text":"Referred to the House Committee on Financial Services."},"number":"HR 4989","policyArea":"Housing and Community Development","ranked":true,"stage":"introduced","summary":"Requires the Secretaries of Housing and Urban Development and Agriculture to enter into a memorandum of understanding to streamline housing projects funded by both departments, establish an advisory working group, and report recommendations to Congress within one year.","summarySource":"ai","title":"Streamlining Rural Housing Act of 2025","type":"hr","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/4989"},{"bipartisan":false,"cosponsors":1,"crossPartyCosponsors":0,"id":"hr4737-119","introducedDate":"2025-07-23","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-07-23","text":"Referred to the House Committee on Energy and Commerce."},"number":"HR 4737","policyArea":"Health","ranked":true,"stage":"introduced","summary":"Amends the Federal Food, Drug, and Cosmetic Act to require labeling disclosure when fruits and vegetables bear certain shelf-life-extending product coatings, including those made by Apeel Sciences, with implementation one year after enactment.","summarySource":"ai","title":"Apeel Reveal Act of 2025","type":"hr","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/4737"},{"bipartisan":false,"cosponsors":8,"crossPartyCosponsors":0,"id":"hr3787-119","introducedDate":"2025-06-05","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-06-12","text":"Sponsor introductory remarks on measure. (CR H2661)"},"number":"HR 3787","policyArea":"Economics and Public Financ